diff --git a/docs/running.md b/docs/running.md
index d487725..a56c917 100644
--- a/docs/running.md
+++ b/docs/running.md
@@ -31,13 +31,14 @@ error: missing ROM files; see docs/running.md for the expected set
   --verify              re-run every recompiled block in the interpreter and compare
   --dump-misses FILE    write interpreted entry points for the recompiler
   --scale N             window scale (default 3)
+  --fullscreen          start fullscreen (F11 or Alt+Enter toggles)
 ```
 
 Frame numbers count 59.19 Hz video frames from power-on. The MVS BIOS eyecatcher finishes at about frame 600, and Metal Slug's title appears at about frame 1200.
 
 ## Windowed play
 
-Keys: arrows; **Z X C V** = A B C D; **5** = coin; **1** = start (P1); **2** = start (P2); **3** = select; **9** = service; **F2** = test switch; **Esc** = quit.
+Keys: arrows; **Z X C V** = A B C D; **5** = coin; **1** = start (P1); **2** = start (P2); **3** = select; **9** = service; **F2** = test switch; **F11** (or **Alt+Enter**) = toggle fullscreen; **Esc** = quit.
 
 Gamepads work beside the keyboard: the first one connected is player 1, the second player 2, and they can be plugged in while the game runs. D-pad or left stick; **A B X Y** (Xbox layout; the same positions on any pad SDL knows) = Neo Geo **A B C D**; **Start** = start; **Back** = coin; **left shoulder** = select. The layout is fixed for now (remapping is on the roadmap). A pad SDL doesn't recognise can be described with the `SDL_GAMECONTROLLERCONFIG` environment variable (SDL's own mapping format). `--mute` turns the sound off; `--wav FILE` writes it to a file, also headless.
 
diff --git a/include/neogeorecomp/bus.h b/include/neogeorecomp/bus.h
